{"text": "Looking at this problem, I need to find **40627866717431 mod 148**.\n\nLet me break down this large number into parts that are easier to work with:\n\n40627866717431 = 40 \u00d7 10\u00b9\u00b2 + 627 \u00d7 10\u2079 + 866 \u00d7 10\u2076 + 717 \u00d7 10\u00b3 + 431\n\nI'll compute each term mod 148, but first I need to find the pattern of powers of 10 modulo 148:\n\n**Finding the pattern of 10^n mod 148:**\n- 10\u00b9 \u2261 10 (mod 148)\n- 10\u00b2 \u2261 100 (mod 148)\n- 10\u00b3 = 1000 \u2261 1000 - 6(148) = 1000 - 888 = **112** (mod 148)\n- 10\u2074 \u2261 10 \u00d7 112 = 1120 \u2261 1120 - 7(148) = **84** (mod 148)\n- 10\u2075 \u2261 10 \u00d7 84 = 840 \u2261 840 - 5(148) = **100** (mod 148)\n- 10\u2076 \u2261 10 \u00d7 100 = 1000 \u2261 **112** (mod 148)\n\nThe pattern repeats with period 3: {112, 84, 100}\n\nSince 10\u00b3 \u2261 112 and 112\u00b2 \u2261 112 (mod 148), we have 10\u2076 \u2261 10\u2079 \u2261 10\u00b9\u00b2 \u2261 **112** (mod 148)\n\n**Now computing each term:**\n\n1) **40 \u00d7 10\u00b9\u00b2:** 10\u00b9\u00b2 \u2261 112, so 40 \u00d7 112 = 4480 \u2261 4480 - 30(148) = **40** (mod 148)\n\n2) **627 \u00d7 10\u2079:** 10\u2079 \u2261 112; 627 \u2261 35 (mod 148)\n   - 35 \u00d7 112 = 3920 \u2261 3920 - 26(148) = **72** (mod 148)\n\n3) **866 \u00d7 10\u2076:** 10\u2076 \u2261 112; 866 \u2261 126 (mod 148)\n   - 126 \u00d7 112 = 14112 \u2261 14112 - 95(148) = **52** (mod 148)\n\n4) **717 \u00d7 10\u00b3:** 10\u00b3 \u2261 112; 717 \u2261 125 (mod 148)\n   - 125 \u00d7 112 = 14000 \u2261 14000 - 94(148) = **88** (mod 148)\n\n5) **431:** 431 \u2261 431 - 2(148) = **135** (mod 148)\n\n**Final sum:**\n40 + 72 + 52 + 88 + 135 = 387\n\n387 = 2(148) + 91 = 296 + 91\n\nTherefore: 387 \u2261 **91** (mod 148)\n\n**ANSWER: 91**", "usage": {"calls": 1, "input_tokens": 1237, "output_tokens": 8455, "cost_usd": 0.04351200000000001, "latency_s": 54.56040334701538}, "model": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "stop_reason": "end_turn"}